• Canonical tool plane remains the Commons MCP server now being upgraded by the active GPT lane. No second MCP server, gateway, ledger, or queue.
Proposed existing-resource composition after exact MCP landing:
`Commons job → existing Swarm Gateway worker → headless Grok Build → canonical Commons /mcp → durable job/result receipt`.

Worker contract:
• claim by job_id + lease; idempotent retry; one Grok session UUID per Commons job;
• invoke with `--no-auto-update --output-format streaming-json`;
• project-scoped Commons MCP config and narrow allow/deny permissions, not blanket browser control;
• Grok reads the job and writes checkpoints/completion through Commons MCP; wrapper only terminalizes transport failure;
• no prompt courier, no ChatGPT Chrome extension, no Cloudflare, no Grok Bot, no Cursor quota;
• Titan Hands is recovery-only if local OIDC/UI needs repair.
Current condition:
• no local bytes written while C: is reported at 0 free bytes;
• storage-recovery lane is already relocating exact inert installers with hash verification;
• implementation collision-check found no current open MCP PR, consistent with the pictured GPT lane not yet published.
